{
  "step_1": "The decision reason can be applied to the decision problem. The relevant information for this reason includes the maximum and minimum outcomes of each lottery. Lottery A has a maximum outcome of 0 Euros and a minimum outcome of -4000 Euros. Lottery B has a maximum outcome of 0 Euros and a minimum outcome of -3000 Euros. Since the maximum outcomes are identical (0 Euros), the comparison shifts to the minimum outcomes. The more favorable (i.e., less negative) minimum outcome is -3000 Euros (Lottery B), which the reason would prefer. Thus, the decision reason would lead to choosing Lottery B.",
