{
  "step_1": "The decision reason can be applied to the decision problem. The relevant information involves comparing the maximum and minimum outcomes of the two lotteries. Lottery A has a maximum outcome of 0 Euros and a minimum outcome of -6000 Euros. Lottery B has a maximum outcome of 0 Euros and a minimum outcome of -3000 Euros. Since the maximum outcomes are identical (0 Euros), the decision reason would compare the minimum outcomes. The more favorable minimum outcome is -3000 Euros (Lottery B), so the decision reason would prefer Lottery B. If both lotteries had identical maximum and minimum outcomes, the reason would be indifferent, but here a preference can be determined based on the minimum outcome.",
